/-!
# Preliminary component actions in B.5.9

The literal LA-action on U=[C_V(O₂(LA)),L], the non-IV equality U=[V,L],
the centralizer-projection proof of A≤L, and assembly of every exact
ComponentActionCase or NaturalSeed are proved in the imported extensions.
The action identifications retain the offender image, the S₅ marking and
one compatible actor on both natural summands.

`PreliminaryActions.preliminary_of_source` assembles the faithful preparation,
exhaustive source comparison and projection arguments for every moved component
and every literal moved section. Neither `Prepared` nor `LocalAlternative` is
an assumption of this theorem. `naturalClosureSetup_of_source` supplies this
universal result and component normality to the actual natural-enlargement
consumer. Final earlier-source discharge and the natural-SL₃ enlargement
remain with their source assembly owners.

The exact retained earlier-source inventory is the full projective-line-correct
B.5.1 implication (owner qt-b05-quasisimple), full B.5.5 implication
(qt-b05-quotient-components), and B.4.8(2) implication
(qt-b-04-natural-extensions / qt-b-04). Their original hypotheses and full
conclusions are retained; no reduced component list is an input. Their final
discharge belongs to qt-b05-general-classification. No separate B.5.2, A.1.31
or I.1.6 implication is assumed. The proofs use checked model ranks, natural
module cohomology, B.1.5 restriction, B.7.2 invariance and the odd-order Irr⁺
centralizer APIs.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
B.5.9, printed pp.107–108. Final natural-SL₃ enlargement is separate.
-/
